fc8a0ac3 pZTlclmkJoZi5N0YAKMbRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 92:82a7616e63686f727391da003f2f55736572732f776f726b73706163652f576f726b73706163652f636170746e2f706b672f636f672f776f726b73706163652e676f3a313a312d3734383a31ac616e737765724c656e677468d10c8d This file implements the cog package's Workspace: an on-disk observation store (captn.cog) plus a file-parsing/graph layer. Key pieces: (1) COGObservation pairs an answer (common.ObservationSchema) with metadata holding anchor FileRanges; Serialize() returns just the answer text. (2) Workspace holds loaded/loading COGFile maps, a mutex, the workspace path, an ObservationCache keyed by hash, an optional git.Repository, ActiveAuthor, and an observationOrder map + counter that preserves insertion order for deterministic serialization. A package-level wspaceCache (guarded by wspaceCacheMux) memoizes Workspaces per path. (3) SetObservationLocked assigns a monotonically increasing write index to new hashes and stores the observation; SetObservation is the mutex-taking wrapper. (4) OpenWorkspace checks the cache, otherwise creates a Workspace, acquires a flock on captn.cog first (comment notes deadlock avoidance), best-effort opens the git repo and reads global git config to build ActiveAuthor as "Name <email>" (Author overrides User), then reads captn.cog if it exists and unmarshals it; on success it caches the workspace. A missing file is not an error. (5) The wire format: each record is "authorHash hash metadata answer\n" where authorHash is a 4-byte hex xxhash32 of the author string, and metadata is "<len>:<hex(msgpack{anchors, answerLength})>". encodeMetadata/decodeMetadata handle this; answers are consumed by byte length (answerLength) so they may contain newlines — unmarshalLocked parses sequentially with strings.Cut rather than splitting lines, validating the author hash (4 bytes), hash, metadata, answer length, and requiring a newline separator after each answer. marshalLocked deterministically indexes any unindexed cache entries (sorted by hash string), sorts all keys by write index, and emits records. Persist marshals under the mutex and writes the file with 0644. LockFile uses flock.TryLock and errors if already locked. (6) LoadFile implements singleflight-style deduplication: it returns cached COGFiles, waits on an in-flight loadFileCall (respecting ctx cancellation), or parses via ParseFile and caches the result; LoadFiles fans out via common.ParallelCollect. (7) SearchSnippet locates a snippet's range in a file, collects AST nodes in that range, gathers call-expression symbol positions, batch-resolves their definitions through an LSP client, resolves each definition to a dependency node in the (preloaded) external file, links each external node to the nearest node-of-interest (functions or module per IsNodeOfInterest) of its internal reference, then builds an ObservationGraph: root module vertex, one vertex per node-of-interest, edges either from the chained upstream node or from the root. (8) queryWithDepth recursively builds an import graph for a *COGFile: it adds the file vertex tagged with its import_type, lists dependencies, and in parallel goroutines loads each import, skips stdlib/package dependencies, adds vertex+edge under a shared mutex, and recurses with depth-1; a visited set and depth guard terminate recursion, and non-COGFile nodes are an error. QueryWithDepth is the public entrypoint that creates the graph and initial visited map.
fc8a0ac3 9e9e5790hDxi5N0YAKMbRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 94:82a7616e63686f727391da00412f55736572732f776f726b73706163652f576f726b73706163652f636170746e2f706b672f636f672f776f726b73706163652e676f3a3134393a312d3233313a32ac616e737765724c656e677468d1053a OpenWorkspace returns a cached *Workspace for the path if one exists in the package-level wspaceCache (guarded by wspaceCacheMux). Otherwise it constructs a new Workspace and immediately acquires a flock on the captn.cog file via LockFile — done before anything else, per the comment, to avoid deadlock; lock failure aborts. It then best-effort opens a git repository at the workspace root (printing a warning and continuing without git on failure) and best-effort loads the global git config through the plugin config loader to derive ActiveAuthor formatted as "Name <email>", where Author.Name/Author.Email override User.Name/User.Email and the field is only set if at least one is non-empty; config errors just print warnings. With the lock deferred for release, it opens captn.cog read-write: os.ErrNotExist returns the fresh empty workspace successfully, any other open error fails. It reads the whole file, then calls unmarshalLocked under wspace.Mux to populate the ObservationCache from the serialized records, wrapping decode failures with the workspace path. Only after successful decode is the workspace stored into wspaceCache and returned. Note the cache check and cache insert are separate lock acquisitions, so two concurrent first-time opens could race (the second would fail LockFile since the file is already flocked).
fc8a0ac3 -0Tm9WEjwYxi5N0YAKMbRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 160: OpenWorkspace loads the workspace's persisted COG data as part of construction: after acquiring the file lock it opens the file at wspace.FilePath() (captn.cog in the workspace root), reads its full contents with io.ReadAll, and hands the bytes to the loaded routine under wspace.Mux. That routine parses the records sequentially — author hash, observation hash, length-prefixed msgpack metadata, then an answer consumed by the byte length recorded in the metadata — and installs each as a COGObservation via SetObservationLocked, preserving on-disk order in observationOrder. OpenWorkspace treats a missing file as an empty workspace, but propagates any parse error wrapped with the workspace path, and only caches the workspace globally after the load succeeds.
